cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Gamut in published work, please cite it as below, and
  name the format version your files declare (the root attribute
  `format`, for example "gamut/1").
title: "Gamut: an open file format for simulation studies"
type: software
version: 2.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-30
authors:
  - name: "Bijective Systems"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bijective-systems-org/gamut"
url: "https://github.com/bijective-systems-org/gamut"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Gamut is an open file format for the results of a parametric
  simulation study and the models fitted to it. One HDF5 file, laid
  out as a valid netCDF-4 file, holds the run table (parameters with
  roles, labels, statuses, splits and scalar results, every number with
  its units), the mesh the fields live on, the fields themselves as one
  block of runs by nodes when the runs share a mesh, uncertainty and
  gradients beside the values they describe, and fitted models in the
  same terms as the data. One C++ core, with Python, MATLAB, Julia, C and
  Rust interfaces, implements the specification, and a shared corpus of
  valid, broken and hostile files holds every language to it.
keywords:
  - simulation data
  - parametric study
  - surrogate model
  - HDF5
  - netCDF-4
  - mesh
  - scientific machine learning
  - uncertainty quantification
